   360:/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   361:   Full card (shared by sub-screens)
   362:   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
   363:/*
   364: * --ledge-space is set while the dog stands on this card's top edge (see useSceneGround).
   365: * The card is a fixed frame (white, rounded, padding kept) holding the back button; only .full-card__scroll scrolls,
   366: * so scrolled content is clipped inside the frame instead of running into the card's edge. (FullCard.tsx)
   367: */
   368:.full-card { top: calc(var(--top-bar-space) + var(--ledge-space, -12px)); display: flex; flex-direction: column; overflow: hidden; }
   369:.full-card > .back-button { flex: none; align-self: flex-start; }
   370:/* Spans the frame's side padding (negative margin + padding) so focus rings and shadows aren't clipped at the content edge. */
   371:.full-card__scroll { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; margin-inline: -20px; padding: 8px 20px; overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; scrollbar-width: none; }
   372:.full-card__scroll::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
   373:.back-button { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; margin: -5px 0 14px -5px; padding: 5px; border: 0; color: var(--color-text-back); background: transparent; font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); cursor: pointer; }
   374:.streak-line { margin: 6px 0 0; color: var(--color-text-body); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); }
   375:.supporting { max-width: 430px; margin: 10px 0 22px; color: var(--color-text-body); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); line-height: 1.45; }
   376:.score-orb { flex: none; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 57px; height: 57px; border-radius: var(--radius-full); color: #204a36; background: var(--color-accent-score); font-weight: var(--font-weight-black); }
   377:
   378:/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
